{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf. The token-taking initializer calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" internally; runtime GDPR \/ diagnostic toggles are methods on the service. The app never needs to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" on the happy path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a step-by-step integration walkthrough, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For value-mapping rules, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Library target","anchor":"Library-target"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Import: ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", package: \"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\"),"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Types","anchor":"Types"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService``","anchor":"docSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsdocumentationSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"code":["public struct MixpanelAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService, @unchecked Sendable {","    \/\/ Identical on every platform.","    public init(","        token: String,","        trackAutomaticEvents: Bool = false,","        flushInterval: Double = 60,","        instanceName: String? = nil,","        optOutTrackingByDefault: Bool = false,","        useUniqueDistinctId: Bool = false,","        deviceIdProvider: (@Sendable () -> String?)? = nil,","        superProperties: [String: AnalyticsValue]? = nil,","        serverURL: String? = nil,","        useGzipCompression: Bool = true,","        excludeProperties: Set<String> = []","    )","","    public init(instance: MixpanelInstance)","","    public func setOptedOut(_ optedOut: Bool) async","    public func optOutTracking() async","    public func optInTracking(distinctID: String? = nil, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]? = nil) async","    public func hasOptedOutTracking() async -> Bool","    public func setLoggingEnabled(_ enabled: Bool) async","    public func setUseIPAddressForGeoLocation(_ enabled: Bool) async","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Value type holding a reference to a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":"; every copy shares the instance. It is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unchecked Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" because the SDK serializes its tracking work on internal queues. The diagnostic setters are the exception — they write properties the SDK doesn’t synchronize, so call them once at launch. Cheap to pass into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK applies most calls later, on its own serial queue, while checking consent on the caller’s thread. The adapter closes the gaps that leaves; each method below says how."}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"code":["public init(token: String, ...)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelOptions"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize(options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" internally, retaining the resulting instance. Parameters mirror "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelOptions"},{"type":"text","text":" — including its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useGzipCompression: true"},{"type":"text","text":" default; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"superProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" takes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[String: AnalyticsValue]"},{"type":"text","text":" so the app does not need to reference "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelType"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIdProvider"},{"type":"text","text":" supplies a custom stable device ID (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the contract: cached value only, no inline I\/O)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Mixpanel SDK keys instances by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"type":"text","text":" (falling back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":"); constructing a second service with the same name returns the existing SDK instance and silently ignores the new options. Services for different projects can safely be built concurrently: the adapter looks its instance up by name, working around an SDK race that could otherwise hand one service the other’s instance. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"superProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" are re-applied after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"type":"text","text":" and after opting back in, since the SDK drops them at both points and ignores them while opted out."}]},{"code":["public init(instance: MixpanelInstance)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Escape hatch for apps that need to build their own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":" (for example, to use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProxyServerConfig"},{"type":"text","text":"). Most apps should prefer the token initializer; this is the only path that requires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" in your app. Super properties registered on such an instance are the app’s to manage."}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"`track(_:) async`","anchor":"track-async"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Forwards to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.track(event:properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Empty "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" are passed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than an empty dictionary, and properties that translate to null are omitted (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Returns immediately; Mixpanel batches and flushes on its own schedule."}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"`identify(userID:properties:) async`","anchor":"identifyuserIDproperties-async"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Forwards to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.identify(distinctId:)"},{"type":"text","text":", then sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" on the user’s profile with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance.people.set(properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; properties that translate to null are unset instead. Empty "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userID"},{"type":"text","text":"s are dropped entirely: the SDK rejects blank distinct IDs, and forwarding the people update anyway would attribute it to the previous identity. Calls made while opted out are dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the user changes, everything queued for the previous user is sent first, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" waits for it — the SDK attributes queued profile updates to whoever is identified when they are sent."}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"`alias(newID:previousID:) async`","anchor":"aliasnewIDpreviousID-async"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Forwards to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.createAlias(_:distinctId:andIdentify:)"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"andIdentify: false"},{"text":", so the alias never changes who is identified locally — the SDK default would re-identify the device as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"previousID"},{"text":", undoing a preceding sign-in. When ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"previousID"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":", the anonymous distinct ID the device’s events were sent under is used. The SDK sends its queue after every alias, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" waits for that so the send can’t overlap the next flush and duplicate rows. Empty ","type":"text"},{"code":"newID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s are dropped, mirroring the SDK’s blank-alias rejection. Projects on Mixpanel’s Simplified ID Merge ignore aliases; see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"`reset() async`","anchor":"reset-async"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sends everything queued and waits for it, then forwards to ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelInstance.reset(completion:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and awaits its callback — the SDK’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends one 50-record batch and deletes the rest. Clears Mixpanel’s local distinct ID, super properties, and timed events, then re-applies the initializer’s super properties. While opted out it leaves the SDK alone: its ","type":"text"},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would also erase the persisted opt-out, and the user would be tracked again from the next launch.","type":"text"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"`flush() async`","anchor":"flush-async"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Forwards to ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelInstance.flush(performFullFlush: true, completion:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and awaits its callback, so the whole queue is sent rather than the SDK’s default 50-record batch. The SDK sends one request per 50 records, each bounded at 120 seconds, and stops at the first failure, so a hung server can hold this for minutes — use the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush(timeout:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on shutdown paths. The SDK delivers the callback on the main queue; never block the main thread waiting for it. The plugin’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the deterministic sync point in tests — it awaits all pending fire-and-forget tracking tasks and then calls this.","type":"text"}]},{"level":4,"text":"`setOptedOut(_:) async`","anchor":"setOptedOut-async","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"optInTracking()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Shaped for the plugin’s "},{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook: "},{"code":"onConsentChange: { await service.setOptedOut($0) }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"text":"`optOutTracking() async`","anchor":"optOutTracking-async","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sends everything queued, resets the local identity, then forwards to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns once the SDK has applied it. From then on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are dropped until ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Does nothing when already opted out. Persists across launches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" delete the user’s Mixpanel profile. The SDK’s own opt-out queues a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$delete"},{"text":" that is never sent and that would later delete the next identified user’s profile; resetting the identity first stops it being queued. Use Mixpanel’s GDPR deletion API from your server to erase data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"text":"`optInTracking(distinctID:properties:) async`","anchor":"optInTrackingdistinctIDproperties-async","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Forwards to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.optInTracking(distinctId:properties:)"},{"text":" and returns once the SDK has applied it, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"text":" issued straight afterwards is honored. The SDK identifies the user as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinctID"},{"text":" (when non-empty) and records a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$opt_in"},{"text":" event carrying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"text":" — they are event properties, not profile properties. The event is queued a moment after the opt-in takes effect, so a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":" issued straight away may leave it for the next one. When the user is already opted in, no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$opt_in"},{"text":" is sent and only the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinctID"},{"text":" identify happens. Before opting in, anything the SDK kept queued while opted out is discarded — only a stale profile deletion or unattributed leftovers can be there. The wait for the SDK is bounded at 30 seconds; hitting the bound logs a fault.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"text":"`hasOptedOutTracking() async -> Bool`","anchor":"hasOptedOutTracking-async-%3E-Bool","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Forwards to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.hasOptedOutTracking()"},{"text":". On a first launch with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"text":", it first waits for the SDK to apply the default — until it does, the SDK reports the user as opted in. (Not with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(instance:)"},{"text":", which doesn’t know the instance’s options.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"text":"`setLoggingEnabled(_:) async`","anchor":"setLoggingEnabled-async","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.loggingEnabled"},{"text":". Useful during development; disable in release. Set it once at launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"text":"`setUseIPAddressForGeoLocation(_:) async`","anchor":"setUseIPAddressForGeoLocation-async","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance.useIPAddressForGeoLocation"},{"text":". Disable when your privacy policy forbids IP-based geo resolution. Set it once at launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/servicereference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Service Reference","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the Mixpanel-backed "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that the analytics plugin consumes."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference"],"anchor":"Reference","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optInTracking","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"distinctID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"properties","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SwiduxAnalytics0B5ValueO","text":"AnalyticsValue","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"title":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Opts the user back into tracking and returns once the SDK has applied","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"text":" issued straight afterwards is honored.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optintracking(distinctid:properties:)"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MockServiceReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockservicereference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — a recording ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"title":"Mock Service Reference","role":"article"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"title":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that owns and forwards to a Mixpanel SDK"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"instance.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToImplementService":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtoimplementservice","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Configure ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to match your privacy, residency, and batching needs — without ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your app.","type":"text"}],"title":"How to Implement the Service","role":"article"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recording "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" for previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockmixpanelanalyticsservice"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ValueTranslation":{"kind":"article","title":"Value Translation","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cases map onto Mixpanel’s "},{"code":"MixpanelType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/valuetranslation"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}